<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 February, from 1249 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mongols" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongols.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1249">1249 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">777 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">André de Longjumeau sets out as Louis IX's envoy to the Mongols</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dominican André de Longjumeau set out as Louis IX's envoy to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, carrying letters and lavish gifts, including a chapel tent of scarlet cloth. From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> the party travelled for a year to the Khan's court.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1270">1270 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">756 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lithuania defeats the Livonian Order on the frozen Baltic Sea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Battle of Karuse, Lithuanian forces decisively defeated the Livonian Order on the frozen sea between the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Muhu</a> and the mainland. The battle was recorded mainly in the Livonian Rhymed Chronicle, which gave it 192 lines.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade">Livonian Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1659">1659 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">367 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earliest surviving English cheque is written</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nicholas Vanacker wrote a cheque for 400 pounds drawn on his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> goldsmith-bankers, Morris and Clayton. It is the oldest known surviving handwritten cheque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1804">1804 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen Decatur burns the captured USS Philadelphia at Tripoli</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lieutenant Decatur and a small crew slipped into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli-greece">Tripoli</a> harbour and set fire to the frigate, captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> state. Nelson is said to have called it the most daring act of the age.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howard Carter opens Tutankhamun's burial chamber</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before invited officials, Carter broke through the sealed wall to reveal a gilded shrine filling the chamber. The king's sarcophagus and gold coffins lay within, untouched for over 3,000 years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wallace Carothers's nylon is patented</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">DuPont received the patent for nylon, invented by a team led by Wallace Carothers. The first fully synthetic fibre, it was used for stockings and then wartime parachutes.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American paratroopers and infantry assault Corregidor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US forces landed by parachute and sea on the island fortress at the mouth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Bay, lost in 1942. After two weeks of fighting most of its Japanese defenders were dead.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First 911 emergency call made in Alabama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Haleyville, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>, Senator Rankin Fite made the first call on the new 911 emergency number. A single, easily remembered number spread across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> over the following decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 February <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nichiren"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nichiren.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nichiren</span><span class="tp">1222–1282</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/coluccio-salutati"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/coluccio-salutati.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Coluccio Salutati</span><span class="tp">1331–1406</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giambattista-bodoni"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giambattista-bodoni.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giambattista Bodoni</span><span class="tp">1740–1813</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
